 # pi-yaams: emit memory bootstrap as a prompt contributor instead of mutating systemPrompt
 
 Owner: Muninn. In ~/git/pi-yaams/index.ts.
 
-- Stop returning { systemPrompt: event.systemPrompt + block } from before_agent_start (discarded by Sandpiper's prompt rebuild).
-- Instead emit a prompt contributor { id: 'yaams-memory-bootstrap', getContent } on the agreed event-bus channel during resources_discover.
-- getContent computes the <memory> block once and caches per session (preserve existing memoryBootstrapCache + fail-closed DB scoping + debug-file behavior).
-- Keep the env gate (YAAMS_BOOTSTRAP_ENABLED) and --memory-guidelines flag semantics.
-- Coordinate channel name + payload shape with Huginn's sandpiper-ai contract.
-- pi-yaams must stay harness-agnostic: guard so the contributor path degrades gracefully when the Sandpiper collector isn't present (plain Pi). Decide whether to keep the legacy systemPrompt-append fallback for non-Sandpiper harnesses.
-
+STATUS 2026-06-09: First pass IMPLEMENTED + verified local (bun test 63/63, tsc clean). HELD at verified-local — do NOT push/merge until AGENT-214 collector confirms it consumes the exact same contract shape.
+
+Shipped shape (candidate contract, pending Huginn ratification in AGENT-214):
+- channel const SANDPIPER_PROMPT_CONTRIBUTOR_EVENT = 'sandpiper:prompt-contributor'
+- payload SandpiperPromptContribution: { id; source; phase?; getContent(): Promise<block>; acknowledge?() }
+- session_start: reset bootstrap cache + collector ack state
+- resources_discover: emit YAAMS bootstrap provider on the channel
+- acknowledge() round-trip resolves the harness-agnostic fallback: collector acks => skip direct before_agent_start mutation; no ack => preserve legacy direct-append for plain Pi / old Sandpiper
+- factored computeMemoryBootstrapPromptBlock() so both paths share cache/debug/DB-fail-closed behavior
+- README updated; tests cover emission, acked-collector path, fallback path
+
+GATE: channel name + payload field names must be identical on both sides or the event-bus handshake silently no-ops. Converge in room before either side hardens.
+
